<title>GREECE: GREEK NATIONAL MORTGAGE BANK SETS RATES ON ITS BONDS.</title>
<headline>GREEK NATIONAL MORTGAGE BANK SETS RATES ON ITS BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's state National Mortgage Bank said in a statement that its bonds which mature on September 30 will be renewed for one year at 14.60 percent.</p>
<p>Its September 1996 bonds will feature a rate of 14.60 percent subject to a 15 percent withholding tax, the National Mortgage Bank said in a statement. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
